# The star's theme, from AXI. Plays when she is out of lives and the star
# comes out of the distance, and again at the end of the demo.
#
# It is the only music in the game with no drums. The overworld skips and the
# King marches; this one is being spoken to kindly after losing, and a kit
# under that turns consolation into a results screen.
#
# Short on purpose. The scene it plays under is four and a half seconds: what
# the player hears is the opening phrase, so the opening phrase has to be the
# whole idea rather than a run-up to one.
#
# C major, 100 BPM, 4 bars, 4/4. 16bit, like everything AXI ships.

@track star-axi
  name   THE STAR (AXI)
  bpm    100
  beats  16
  era    16bit
  tags   axi game original

# A bell, falling and then lifting on the last bar -- "there, there" and then
# "off you go". Long notes: at four bars there is no room to be busy.
@voice lead inst=fm-bell mix=0.20
  g4  .   .   .   .   .   e4  .   .   .   .   .   c4  .   .   .
  d4  .   .   .   .   .   f4  .   .   .   .   .   e4  .   .   .
  a4  .   .   .   .   .   g4  .   .   .   .   .   e4  .   .   .
  f4  .   .   .   g4  .   .   .   c5  .   .   .   .   .   .   .

# Held rather than moving. The overworld's chord turns over every sixteenth,
# which is what makes it bright; this one sits under the bell and stays put.
@voice pad inst=arp mix=0.035
  c   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  dm  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  am  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  f   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   g   .   .   .   .   .   .   .

# Two notes a bar, low and slow. A walking bass would put it back on its feet
# and this is the one moment in the game that is allowed to sit down.
@voice bass inst=tri mix=0.15
  c2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   g2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  d2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   a2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  a1  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   e2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
  f2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .   g2  .   .   .   .   .   .   .
